  "body": "Found by the #926 per-post script suites (recorded stream `drill_retract`: two pecked holes, R plane Z1, hop between holes Z3, clearance Z10).\n\n**What is wrong.** The canned-cycle posts - `fanuc`, `haas`, `mazak`, `sinumerik`, `tormach`, `doosan-dnm` - move from one hole to the next at the R plane, not at the hop / clearance height the toolpath (and so verify and the stock simulation) uses:\n\n```\nG00 X10 Y10 Z1          <- the stream's rapid down to R is posted before the cycle\nG98                     <- \"return to the initial level\" - which is now Z1, the R plane\nG73 X10 Y10 Z-20 R1 Q4 F60\nG80\nG73 X30 Y10 Z-15 R1 Q4 F60   <- X10 -> X30 traverse at Z1; the path hops at Z3\n```\n\nThe cycle swallows the chain's hop rapids (`Rapid Z3`, `Rapid X30 Z3`, `Rapid Z1`), and G98 returns to the level the tool stood at when the first cycle block was read. `fanuc.cps` says \"The chain retracts to its initial (clearance) level each hole\", but the dump posts move 0 (the rapid from clearance down to R) as an ordinary G00 before the cycle record (AT 1), so the initial level is R. Sinumerik writes no G98/G99 at all and lands the same way. The committed app golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/drill_plate.nc` already shows it: R0 there, so the posted program rapids from X10 to X30 at Z0 - the stock top - while `drill_plate.cl` hops at Z5.\n\nWhy P0: the posted traverse is lower than the motion that was simulated and judged. A hop height exists to clear something between holes (a clamp, a boss, stock above the model top); the program drives through it at rapid.\n\nHeidenhain and Carvera post the expanded chain and are correct.\n\nDone means: every canned-cycle post traverses between holes at the stream's hop level and leaves the last hole at its retract (e.g. initial level = the hop/clearance plane with G98, or G99 with the R plane and an explicit hop), pinned by the #926 `drill_retract` goldens of all six posts (now listed as known bugs in `crates/post/tests/recorded/mod.rs`) and the app golden `nc/drill_plate.nc`.\n",
